  "contentCreated": "2005-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "origin": "Audio transcripts of 2,063,066 videos shared on YouTube under the CC-BY license, comprising 22,709,724 original and automatically translated transcripts from 3,156,703 videos across 721,136 individual channels (~45 billion words). Original-language content is majority English (71%); automated translations provided in English, French, Spanish, German, Russian, Italian, and Dutch. Every YouTube channel is credited in accordance with CC-BY attribution requirements. Form: audio transcribed + multilingual translation added. Note: the originator here is a very large set of individual, mostly non-institutional creators (721,136 channels) rather than a single institution — unlike the other Common Corpus records, this tests whether a single creator entry can stand for a large distributed creator population, or whether the schema needs a way to point at a creator manifest/roster. See notes/stress-test-pleias-common-corpus.md (Gap C). Attribution per-channel is provided in the dataset metadata, but a ProvenanceRecord.creator[] entry cannot enumerate 721k individual creators; the single originator entry above is a best-effort summary, not a complete attribution.",
  "custodyChain": [
    {
      "agent": "https://www.youtube.com/",
      "action": "individual-creators-published-videos-under-cc-by",
      "startTime": "2005-01-01T00:00:00Z"
    },
    {
      "agent": "https://huggingface.co/PleIAs",
